# --- Large / regenerable data files ---
# Raw source extracts (106MB total) - see README "Reproducing the data" section
# for exact download/regeneration steps. Not committed to keep the repo light
# and because these are third-party FOI/Contracts Finder exports, not code.
data/raw/*.csv

# Large derived outputs (regenerated by `python -m src.run_pipeline` in ~40s).
# master_procurement_panel.csv (~79MB), anomaly_scores.csv (~38MB) and
# validation_redflags.csv (~94MB) are all close to GitHub's 100MB per-file
# limit and provide no review value as raw dumps - the small summary CSVs
# below (data_quality_report, hhi_monthly*, new_supplier_rate_by_month,
# shap_top_anomalies, spend_distribution_by_period, stl_decomposition,
# stl_shock_summary) ARE committed since they're <50KB and directly support
# the report's figures/tables.
data/processed/master_procurement_panel.csv
data/processed/anomaly_scores.csv
data/processed/validation_redflags.csv

